---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { leaders } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="TurbineBridge finds used turbines of all kinds. Some new systems are five years out. We connect the specialists who bring a used unit back online."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="The company"
    title="Find the turbine. Connect the people who can run it."
    lede="We find a used unit of any class that can be brought back online, and we connect you with the specialists who put it in shape to run. Some new systems are five years out. Plenty are not."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="block-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Story</p>
        <h2>The party in the middle</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          A plant that needs power and a used turbine that can still be saved are often in different hands. TurbineBridge finds the machine and introduces the specialists. That is the work. We do not own the shop, and we do not sign the engineering.
        </p>
        <p>
          The people we call have three decades in the power industry. That is how we know who handles each part of the repair, from the rotating equipment to the control unit that starts, fuels, and protects the turbine.
        </p>
        <p>
          The customers are industrial plants, data centers, utilities, and other loads that need a unit sooner than a new-equipment queue. Some turbine systems are five years out. Others are not. We take all kinds of units, as long as specialists can bring them back online.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="block-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">The desk</p>
        <h2>Who you reach.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        {leaders.map((person) => (
          <article class="card">
            <p class="eyebrow">{person.role}</p>
            {"detail" in person && person.detail ? <p class="role-detail">{person.detail}</p> : null}
            <h3>{person.name}</h3>
            {person.phone ? (
              <p><a class="link" href={`tel:${person.tel}`}>{person.phone}</a></p>
            ) : (
              <p><a class="link" href={`/contact?interest=${encodeURIComponent("Something else")}&who=${encodeURIComponent(person.name)}`}>Write {person.name.split(" ")[0]}</a></p>
            )}
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="block-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Purpose</p>
        <h2>Mission and vision</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-2">
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Mission</p>
          <h3>Find the unit. Make the introduction.</h3>
          <p>
            Find a used turbine the load can use, in any class, and introduce the specialists who can bring it online.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Vision</p>
          <h3>The desk for the wait, and for every other unit</h3>
          <p>
            Be the desk people call when a new system is years out, and when any used unit needs the right shop.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="block-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">How the work is paid for</p>
        <h2>Engagement structures</h2>
        <p class="measure">These are the ways TurbineBridge expects to be paid.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stack">
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>Equipment sales and brokerage fees</li>
          <li>Procurement and transaction management fees</li>
          <li>Advisory and consulting services</li>
          <li>Long-term service and support partnerships</li>
          <li>Potential equity participation in select projects</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="measure">
          Nothing on this site is an offer to sell a security. Any participation structure is discussed directly with the company.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="block-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">From here</p>
        <h2>How the work grows</h2>
        <p class="measure">Each engagement is a found unit and an introduction. The rest follows from doing that well.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timeline">
        <article class="timeline-item">
          <h3>1. Keep the network in working order</h3>
          <p>The people we call already span three decades in the power industry. The plan is to keep those specialist relationships sharp, including the shops that handle control units.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="timeline-item">
          <h3>2. Find the unit, then make the introduction</h3>
          <p>That pair of steps is the engagement. The class of machine can change. The job does not.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="timeline-item">
          <h3>3. Deepen the service relationships</h3>
          <p>Stay close to the shops that can bring a used turbine back online, so the introduction between a machine and a specialist gets faster.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="timeline-item">
          <h3>4. Wider site work comes after the machine</h3>
          <p>
            A fuller power solution for the site is later work. It does not make TurbineBridge the engineer of record.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="timeline-item">
          <h3>5. Let finished work earn the next one</h3>
          <p>The same standard goes further only after the units already handled have earned that trust.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="block-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Values</p>
        <h2>What we will be held to</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Integrity</h3>
          <p>The condition is stated as found, including what the record does not show.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Reliability</h3>
          <p>The introduction still holds after the first call.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Technical Excellence</h3>
          <p>The iron and the control unit each get a specialist who works that class.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Customer Focus</h3>
          <p>The load, the site, and the date set the search.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Sustainability</h3>
          <p>A unit returned to service is preferred when it can do the duty.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Long-Term Partnerships</h3>
          <p>We stay in the middle until the unit can go online, and after that if you want us there.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="cta-inner">
      <h2>Bring the site into the conversation.</h2>
      <p>A machine class or a load is enough to begin. We read every note and reply with the right next step.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact">Send an inquiry</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
